 "question": "Is the simulator's range the right width?",
 "headline": "With demand noise at the assumed 3% a month, the simulator's 80% range held 25 of United's 33 unit-revenue outcomes in 2022-2026 (76%, against a nominal 80%); a value fitted on 2013-2019 (0.29%) held 20 (61%), so the assumption is kept.",
 "plain_summary": [
  "With demand noise at the assumed 3% a month, the simulator's 80% range held 25 of United's 33 unit-revenue outcomes in 2022-2026 (76%, against a nominal 80%); a value fitted on 2013-2019 (0.29%) held 20 (61%), so the assumption is kept.",
  "The question is whether the simulator's range is the right width.",
  "Compared: how far United's revenue per seat mile landed from a naive forecast made two, three and four quarters earlier (last year's quarter, moved by the latest year-over-year growth), against the gap between two simulated worlds at the same distance.",
  "Roughly 8 in 10 is read as 70% to 90% inside: on 2022-2026 the assumed value passes and the fitted value fails.",
  "On 2013-2019 the assumed value held 63 of 63 (100%), which is too wide for those years; the fitted value held 48 of 63 (76%) there.",
  "The value tried and set aside is 0.29% a month, where the simulator matches the 2013-2019 spread. Leaving out any one year gives 0.00% to 0.73%; if every surprise were demand it would be 2.49%.",
  "Operating margin, same comparison: the simulator's 80% range holds 42 of 42 (100%) outcomes in 2016-2019, which is too wide, and 28 of 33 (85%) in 2022-2026, which is about right.",
  "Simulated margin gaps are 2.9 times the earlier spread two quarters out and 1.9 times at four; against the later one, 1.0 and 1.0 times.",
  "Fuel volatility, not demand noise, sets most of the width. The no-shock range for 2026Q4 operating income is $2,455 million wide (P10 to P90). With demand noise switched off it is still $2,298 million (94%); with fuel noise switched off it is $1,557 million (63%).",
  "Fuel volatility is measured over the 65 trading days before the cutoff (13 April 2026 to 16 July 2026). That stretch was 2.3 times as volatile as 2013-2019 and more volatile than 92% of such windows since 2013.",
  "Simulated fuel-price gaps are 1.6 times the 2013-2019 spread two quarters out and 1.1 times at four; against 2022-2026, 1.3 and 1.1 times.",
  "The no-shock range for 2026Q4 operating income is -$160 million to $2,296 million; the fitted value would make it -$113 million to $2,152 million, 8% narrower.",
  "At today's fuel price ($4.67 a gallon paid), 37.9% of simulated runs have negative free cash flow over 12 months with measured behavior; the fitted value would make it 34.6%."
 ],
